use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/FormParticipation import FormParticipation
from ../../../behaviors/Presence import Presence
from ../../../behaviors/Selection import Selection
from ../../../behaviors/Traversal import Traversal
from ../../collections/List import List
from ../../overlays/Popover import Popover

export ui-component CascadeSelect:
    description:
        A cascade select lets the user pick one value from options arranged in
        levels, such as a country, then a region, then a city. It works like a
        Select, but choosing an option that has options under it opens the next
        level beside it, until the user reaches the one they want.

    composes:
        - @{Popover}
        - @{List}

    behaviors:
        - @{Selection}
        - @{Traversal}
        - @{FormParticipation}
        - @{Presence}

    value:
        The value is the picked option together with the path to it, such as
        Europe, France, Paris. When closed, it shows that path, or a
        placeholder if there is no value. How the path is written out is up to
        the component.

    levels:
        Opening it shows the top level as a list. Moving to an option that has
        options under it opens that next level as another list beside it, and
        so on. Only one branch is open at each level at a time. When it opens
        with a value, the levels leading to that value are already open and it
        is highlighted.

    choosing:
        By default only options with nothing under them can be picked, and
        picking one sets the value and closes every level. The component can
        also allow picking an option that has options under it. Escape closes
        every level without changing the value, and focus goes back to the
        cascade select.

    keyboard:
        Up and Down move through the current level, and Home and End go to its
        first and last option. Right, or Enter, on an option with options under
        it opens the next level and moves into it. Left goes back to the level
        before and closes the one that was open. Left on the top level closes
        the cascade select. For right-to-left languages, Left and Right swap.

    pointer:
        Clicking an option with options under it opens the next level. The
        component decides whether just pointing at it does the same, as in a
        menu. If it does, moving the pointer across to the new level doesn't
        close it on the way.

    placement:
        Each new level appears beside the one before, and all of them are kept
        on screen as Positioning describes. What happens when the levels are
        too wide to fit side by side is up to the chosen library.

    accessibility:
        Assistive tools are told which level the highlighted option is in, and
        whether it has options under it and if they are open.

    options:
        Disabled options are shown but can't be picked or opened. Typing
        letters jumps to a matching option in the current level.

    nonGoals:
        - Not for picking several values
        - No typing to search across all levels. That's a Combobox over a
            flattened list
        - Not a menu of commands. Its options are values, not actions
